    "notes": {
        "table": [
            "The cartridge look (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-cartridge-theme.md): an old console's menus after tsubi.club, flat and dark, square boxes with one chamfered corner, 1px outlines, insets rather than casts, and the palette's primary as the one accent. Colours stay palette roles, so matugen drives it like every other table; a flat teal wallpaper gives the reference's home page."
        ],
        "fonts": [
            "Archivo for words and headings (the surfaces set its width and weight axes), DotGothic16 for values and status lines, BIZ UD Mincho for secondary lines. All four families ship with the shell (nix/cartridge-fonts.nix, the tarball), each falling back to its generic alias when missing."
        ],
        "roles.backdrop.grid": [
            "The reference's grid: 2px lines every 120px in the foreground at 0.14, fading out over the bottom fifth (`fade`). Pitch and width are logical pixels; the pass multiplies them by the output's scale. It draws only where `theme.grid` (or `wallpaper.grid`, `lock.grid`) is on, which this preset turns on; the other tables carry the same numbers for anyone who turns it on there."
        ],
        "roles.backdrop.shards": [
            "The animated backdrop's sculpture (`wallpaper.animate`), drawn at half the output's pixels. `fill` is a tint laid over the wallpaper's own mean colour, so the shards read as a facet of whatever is under them, the way the reference's #33504a sits on its #2e4a44; `border` is the edge drawn along each shard's long side, at half-resolution pixels; `ink` is a face turned to the viewer. The other tables carry the same numbers for anyone who turns `wallpaper.animate` on there."
        ],
        "roles.backdrop.mark": [
            "The giant faint mark under the sculpture: the reference's tilted ring and the stacked word inside it, in the background colour at 0.16."
        ],
        "roles.boot": [
            "The boot sequence (`habits.boot`) on its black stage: `fill` is the emblem's rings and wordmark, `border` the grid lines growing in from the edges. White, since the stage is black in either mode. The other tables carry the same numbers for a table that turns a boot on."
        ],
        "roles.cursor": [
            "No ring and no halo: the cursor is a block on the row's leading edge (`cursor.bar`) over a faint primary fill, travelling between rows; in a grid it is two arcs held outside the cell with a glow (`cursor.brackets`)."
        ],
        "roles.hero": [
            "A panel's hero framed in the accent with one chamfered corner, its label on a slanted tab over the frame (`hero.tab`). The primary action is a pill ending in a hexagonal cap holding its icon (`button.default.cap`)."
        ],
        "roles.panel": [
            "The console header (`panel: console`): the title wide and heavy, the `// subtitle` condensed in the accent with a glow, the status strip a pill outlined in the accent, the id strip down the card's leading side behind a line that also outlines the card, and section labels as field tags fading out to the right."
        ],
        "roles.input": [
            "A sunk well: the page colour with a 2px inset shade along its top, and no halo on focus."
        ],
        "motion": [
            "Two clocks carry the look: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) for a card sliding in and a toast arriving, and a spring with real overshoot (CSS linear() peaking at 1.42) for the pile closing up.",
            "The catalogue past the clocks (spec C5), each read off tsubi.club: a focused label widens to 125, 700 and 0.04em over 200ms (`focusText`); hero titles, the status strip and changed values type in on steps(20) over 0.6s (`reveal: type`); rows rise 40px, 60ms apart, on the emerge clock (`arrive.rise`, `arrive.stagger`); a replaced body jumps 10px back and out in two steps, then comes in from 20px (`swap: glitch`); an activated row leaves a ghost scaling to (1.1, 1.3) as it fades over 0.4s (`use`); a field's error label jitters its axes over 0.5s (`error: shake`); a changed picture lands from 20 times its size in two steps (`picture: zoom`); a fresh card's grain fades over 1s (`noise`); progress reads as ten blocks and a percentage (`progress: blocks`). None of them runs at rest."
        ],
        "habits": [
            "A card slides 40px in along its line and fades (`emerge: slide`), panels take the console grammar, launcher grids draw hexagonal tiles, and the session opens on the boot sequence."
        ]
    }
}
